{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2152-07-14 21:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. You’re here because of severe muscle weakness. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2152-07-14 21:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been feeling weaker every day for about a week. I usually walk around my house, but now I can barely stand without holding onto something."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2152-07-14 21:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds really tough. Does this feel like any of your past flare-ups with polymyositis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2152-07-14 21:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly like them. I’ve been in remission for years, but this feels just like before—my arms and legs are so weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2152-07-14 21:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Your blood test from the clinic showed a very high muscle enzyme level—CK was 2550. That confirms this is likely a flare of your polymyositis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2152-07-14 21:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s high. I didn’t feel much better after the steroid shot in the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2152-07-14 21:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It takes time. We’re starting you on strong IV steroids for three days to calm the inflammation. You may not feel better right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2152-07-14 21:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I also feel a bit short of breath. Not terrible—maybe a 3 out of 10—but it’s there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2152-07-14 21:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we noticed some fluid overload. You got a diuretic in the ER and passed over 5 liters of urine. Your lungs have mild congestion, but no pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2152-07-14 21:57:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ve had heart failure flares before. I used to take torsemide, but I stopped months ago because of my job."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2152-07-14 21:59:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand. For now, we’re monitoring you closely. You’re on CPAP at night, which helps with breathing and heart strain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2152-07-14 22:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And I haven’t been taking my warfarin the past few days because I was so weak and couldn’t get to the pharmacy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2152-07-14 22:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR was low at 1.4, so we restarted warfarin. We’re not using IV heparin to bridge, but your clinic will watch your levels closely after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2152-07-14 22:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make sure to follow up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2152-07-15 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from this morning show your CK is coming down—from 2500 to 955. That’s a good sign the steroids are working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2152-07-15 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! Do you think I’ll be able to walk better soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2152-07-15 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It will take time. We’re transitioning you from IV steroids to oral prednisone—60 mg daily. You’ll stay on that for a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2152-07-15 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember prednisone makes my blood sugar go up. I have diabetes too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2152-07-15 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ve been managing your sugars with insulin in the hospital. But since you prefer not to use insulin at home, we’re adding metformin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2152-07-15 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can take that. But will it be enough with the steroids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2152-07-15 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re restarting your glipizide and liraglutide too. Metformin will help extra. Your PCP can adjust doses later if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2152-07-15 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds good. My blood pressure has been high too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2152-07-15 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been up to 190s over 120s. Steroids can make that worse. We’re keeping your metoprolol and increasing losartan from 25 to 50 mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2152-07-15 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep an eye on it at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2152-07-15 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The rheumatology team met with you earlier. They’re restarting mycophenolate—Cellcept—twice a day to help control your polymyositis long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2152-07-15 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I took that before. Is Rituximab also coming back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2152-07-15 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’re considering it. You’ll discuss that with your rheumatologist at your follow-up. For now, we’re focused on getting the flare under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2152-07-15 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. Will I need to take antibiotics too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2152-07-15 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re starting Bactrim—one tablet daily—to prevent a lung infection called PJP, which can happen with high-dose steroids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2152-07-15 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that. I used to take it three times a week, but daily is easier to remember."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2152-07-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Your breathing is better, your heart function is stable, and your weakness is slowly improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2152-07-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can lift my arms better. But I still need help standing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2152-07-16 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. We’ll keep working on it. Your discharge is planned for tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2152-07-16 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What will my meds be at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2152-07-16 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take prednisone 60 mg daily, mycophenolate twice a day, Bactrim daily, and your usual diabetes meds plus new metformin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2152-07-16 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood pressure med is now 50 mg losartan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2152-07-16 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. And warfarin every day. Please follow up with your clinic to check your INR—it was still low this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2152-07-16 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ll also see my rheumatologist soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2152-07-16 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, to plan your steroid taper and discuss Rituximab. We’ll send all the details to your doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2152-07-17 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Keep using your BiPAP at night, take all your medications, and call if you feel worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2152-07-17 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much more stable than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2152-07-17 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re glad the treatment helped. Rest, follow up, and take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2152-07-14 21:40:00",
    "admission_end": "2152-07-17 16:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of polymyositis, morbid obesity, interstitial lung disease, diastolic heart failure, type 2 diabetes, and recurrent venous thromboembolism was admitted for diffuse muscle weakness concerning for a polymyositis flare. She had elevated CK and CRP, was treated with three days of IV methylprednisolone, then transitioned to oral prednisone and mycophenolate. Her weakness improved, and CK decreased. She also had acute on chronic heart failure with mild dyspnea and fluid overload, managed with IV lasix and optimization of home medications. Hypertension was worsened by steroids and addressed by increasing losartan. Warfarin was restarted after a period of underuse. She was started on Bactrim for PJP prophylaxis and metformin for steroid-induced hyperglycemia. She was discharged home on a new medication regimen with close follow-up planned with rheumatology and her primary care team.",
    "problems": [
      "Polymyositis with respiratory involvement",
      "Acute on chronic diastolic (congestive) heart failure",
      "Interstitial pulmonary disease, unspecified",
      "Body mass index [BMI] 70 or greater, adult",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus without complications",
      "Morbid (severe) obesity due to excess calories",
      "Hypertensive heart disease with heart failure",
      "Personal history of other venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Long term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Underdosing of anticoagulants, initial encounter",
      "Patient's intentional underdosing of medication regimen for other reason",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult) (pediatric)",
      "Allergy, unspecified, initial encounter",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated"
    ]
  }
}
